## Windows Command Line

This week I also practiced Windows command-line administration.

### System Identification

`hostname`

Shows the name of the computer.

Mental association:

`hostname` → Which computer am I on?

---

`winver`

Shows:

- Windows edition
- Windows version
- OS build

Useful when checking compatibility or troubleshooting update/version issues.

---

`whoami`

Shows which user account is currently being used.

---

`whoami /all`

Shows more detailed security information including:

- username
- SID
- group memberships
- privileges

Mental association:

`hostname` → which computer?  
`whoami` → which user?

